  "summary": "Preprints now link direct lncRNA targeting and REV-ERB agonism to altered transcriptional programs in cancer and drug-response models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is perturbation of RNA-based and transcriptional regulation in cancer and disease models. Two items target long noncoding RNAs: depleting NRF2-induced NMRAL2P reduces non-small cell lung cancer proliferation and increases cisplatin sensitivity, while CD44-DT binds PCNA and AR to promote p21 degradation and suppress senescence in prostate cancer, where an RNA-PROTAC drives chimeric ncRNA-mediated AR degradation. STL1267, a REV-ERB agonist, alters HIF-1α and REV-ERBα localization and an ATF4-linked metabolic program in CoCl2-treated HeLa cells. A single-cell RNA-seq study of iPSC-derived cultures from 49 individuals maps eQTLs and drug-response eQTLs for ALK inhibitor effects. The cervical cancer item contributes a 12-gene neuroimmune signature. The advance lies in direct lncRNA targeting and genotype-dependent drug-response mapping at single-cell resolution.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
